  "body": "## What changed\n\nA Bore op (or Drill, or Thread) whose hole list was edited to a value off the 1 um lattice - the issue's floor typed as `0.190 in - 0.040 in` = `3.8099999999999996` mm - read **Stale** after save and reopen. The file stores the hole as `3.81` (`HoleDto::from_hole` snaps to the lattice), but the stamp taken at generate hashed the unsnapped bits.\n\n- New `crates/app/src/operation/hole_digest.rs`: one hole (and one radial hole) digested with every float snapped by `cl::lattice`, the same snap `HoleDto` / `CrossHoleDto` apply when the file writes the list. The radial `dir` stays verbatim, as the file keeps it. Byte order per hole is unchanged.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/params.rs`: the Drill (holes + cross), Bore and Thread arms of `stamp_with` call it instead of hashing raw bits (the file shrinks by 28 lines).\n- On-lattice holes (everything `detect_holes` emits) hash bit-for-bit as before, so no stamp that matched before changes. A change of half a micron or more still moves the stamp (unit-pinned). No project-file version bump, no posted-output change, no golden or snapshot change.\n- Same remedy as #1351 / PR #1352 (`path_sig` hashes moves on the lattice). Snapping at the edit command, the brief's first preference, was dropped: the snap would have to be repeated at every door a hole list comes through (create, edit, paste, GUI table, scripts, old files) and would move the generator's input - the reason #1352 dropped snapping in `Toolpath::new`. Recorded in `docs/decisions/1560-hole-digest-lattice.md`.\n\n## Pins (mutation-checked: `put` hashing raw bits -> all three red; restored -> green)\n\n- `bore_entry::an_edited_hole_floor_off_the_lattice_stays_ok_through_save_and_load` - through the commands: `CreateOperation` Bore, `EditOperationParams` with the off-lattice floor, `GenerateOperation`, `project::save`, `project::load` into a fresh world -> `OpStatus::Ok` (mutant: `Stale`).\n- `bore_core::an_edited_hole_floor_off_the_lattice_reopens_ok_and_posts_the_same` - the issue's MCP flow: `detect_holes`, `edit_operation` with `floor_z` 3.8099999999999996 / blind, `generate`, `post` (Fanuc), `save_project`, `open_project` in a new server -> `get_job` status `ok` (mutant: `stale`), and the posted program after reopen is byte-identical to the one before the save.\n- `operation::hole_digest::tests::a_typed_floor_stamps_like_the_one_the_file_reloads` - typed and reloaded floors digest alike; 3.81 vs 3.811 still differ.\n\n## Sweep (other DTOs that call `lattice(...)` at save)\n\n- Params: only `HoleDto` and `CrossHoleDto` snap at save - both covered here (Drill holes + radial holes, Bore, Thread). Every other params float is written verbatim (serde's shortest form round-trips the bits, #169).\n- Cached-output DTOs (`MoveDto`, `CompSpanDto`, the drill-cycle DTO, `ThreadCycleDto`, the edge-break DTO) store a generated cache, not stamp inputs. The moves feed `path_sig`, already lattice since #1352; nothing else digests the spans, cycles or breaks (grepped every `Hasher` user in `crates/app/src`). No follow-up issue needed.\n\n## Gates\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (macOS, sccache): green - wall 10.1 min, 2 steps, 0 failed (it ran every app/ui suite the gate maps name for `app::operation`).\n- Named suites, again on their own: app lib (238), project_roundtrip (73), bore_core (5), bore_entry (4), face_holes, operations, mcp, commands_undo, posting, float_roundtrip - 514 passed, 0 failed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- Fork synced at upstream/main c00ba18a.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- A file already saved before this fix, with a stamp taken from an off-lattice hole, still reads Stale once on reopen; one regenerate stores the new stamp (no re-stamp on load, by design).\n- The GUI hole table (it goes through the same `EditOperationParams` and the same stamp).\n- Batch and release tiers; Windows.\n\nChangelog: An operation whose hole list was edited to a value off the 1 um grid (e.g. an inch floor) no longer reads Stale after save and reopen (#1560)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #1560\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
